1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
R-GUARD hybrid ransomware defense demo
Server-Agent architecture with Behavioral + Decoy trap detection

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Agent collects endpoint telemetry and monitors decoy files
Server performs ML inference and containment decisions

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Decoy placement: finance-like bait files are created
Examples: DEC0Y_finance_00.xlsx, DEC0Y_finance_01.xlsx

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Trap integrity manifest (.decoy_manifest.json)
Stores SHA-256 hash + size for tamper detection

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Any unauthorized modify/delete/encrypt pattern on decoys
raises wiretrap signal for immediate investigation

6
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Server starts on port 8000
Agent heartbeat and detect requests begin streaming

7
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Dashboard opened: live system health + threat intelligence
All panels update from backend alerts

8
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:45,000
CPU Usage card: current processor load percentage
Green<60, Amber 60-80, Red>80

9
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Memory Usage card: RAM pressure indicator
Higher sustained values can signal stress during attack

10
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Disk Activity card: I/O utilization trend
Ransomware often causes sudden write bursts

11
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Network Traffic card: throughput and anomaly surface
Used to notice unusual communication spikes

12
00:03:45,000 --> 00:04:05,000
System Activity chart:
Blue=CPU, Green=Network, Red=suspicious events

13
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Threat Trend chart:
Hourly suspicious event count and attack surge visibility

14
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Recent Alerts table:
Time, Threat Type, Severity, Status

15
00:04:45,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Notifications panel:
Real-time queue of critical/high/medium events

16
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Safe fake attack starts on decoy directory only
No real ransomware, originals preserved

17
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Script creates .locked copies to emulate encryption behavior
This is controlled and presentation-safe

18
00:05:45,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Agent detects decoy interaction and behavioral anomalies
Server receives /agent/detect payload immediately

19
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Detection metrics explained:
behavioral_score, decoy_score, fused risk_score

20
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Fusion rule:
risk = 0.65*behavioral + 0.35*decoy

21
00:06:45,000 --> 00:07:05,000
If risk >= threshold, alert is ransomware=true
Severity escalates to critical when confidence is high

22
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Containment phase:
Suspicious processes are terminated with allowlist protection

23
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Dashboard receives new critical alert in seconds
Badge count and alert table update live

24
00:07:45,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Alert details panel meaning:
Threat, host, evidence, suggested action, containment notes

25
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Result: attack signal detected early through decoy trap
and validated by behavioral evidence

26
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:45,000
R-GUARD demonstrates low-latency detect + respond workflow
for practical ransomware defense operations
